"sentences and excludes list items and tables. Numerals "
"are also entirely ignored and subtracted from the total "
"word count. These settings used specifically for this "
"test may differ from the analysis configurations used for "
"other tests."
msgstr ""

#: results-format/readability_messages.h:517
msgid ""
"A unit is a section of text ending with a period, "
"exclamation mark, question mark, interrobang, colon, "
"semicolon, or dash. Lengthy, complex sentences generally "
"contain more than one unit."
msgstr ""

#: results-format/readability_messages.h:526
msgid ""
"A predicted cloze score is the estimation of a passage's "
"mean score if it were given as a cloze test to a group of "
"students. Scores range from 0 (zero comprehension) to 100 "
"(total comprehension)."
msgstr ""

#: results-format/readability_messages.h:535
msgid ""
"A DRP score measures the difficulty of text in DRP units. "
"These units range from 0 (easy) to 100 (difficult). This "
"score can help match a document to a student based on his/"
"her DRP ability score."
msgstr ""

